/-
# Graphplay/Integrations/Hodge.lean

**Hodge theory on hypergraphs and simplicial complexes** — the
combinatorial / discrete Hodge decomposition, equitable partitions
compatible with the cochain complex, the harmonic-subspace quotient
theorem, persistent-Hodge / TDA connection, and the engineering
payoffs (topological data analysis with equitable speedup, harmonic
topological-qubit encoding, PST in the Hodge setting).

This file is a **statement-only scaffold**.  The proofs are `sorry`;
the structural goal is to (a) define the right types so that downstream
files in Graphplay can refer to them, and (b) state the headline
theorems precisely enough that a future proof effort can fill them in.

Conventions follow `Graphplay.Relational`:

* hypergraphs live as `RelStructure (Signature.kUniform k) V`;
* the hypergraph Laplacian and incidence matrices are the ones already
  defined in `Hypergraph.incidence` and `Hypergraph.laplacian`;
* the equitable-partition machinery is the `RelEquitablePartition`
  one from `Relational.lean`;
* quantum-walk evolution is `WeightedGraph.evolve`.

## References

* B. Eckmann, *Harmonische Funktionen und Randwertaufgaben in einem
  Komplex*, Comment. Math. Helv. 17 (1944/45) — the original discrete
  Hodge theorem.
* L.-H. Lim, *Hodge Laplacians on graphs*, SIAM Review 62 (2020) —
  the modern combinatorial-Hodge framework used here.
* G. Carlsson, *Topology and data*, Bull. AMS 46 (2009) — persistent
  homology / TDA.
* X. Jiang, L.-H. Lim, Y. Yao, Y. Ye, *Statistical ranking and
  combinatorial Hodge theory*, Math. Program. 127 (2011).
* J. Friedman, *Computing Betti numbers via combinatorial
  Laplacians*, Algorithmica 21 (1998).
-/

import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Hermitian
import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialSet.Basic
import Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Module.LinearMap
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs
import Graphplay.Weighted
import Graphplay.Relational

open scoped Matrix
open Complex

universe u v w

namespace Graphplay
